you

3
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:40,750
Krishnamurti in dialogue with Dr. Alan

4
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:44,440
W. Anderson. J. Krishnamurti was born in

5
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:47,040
South India and educated in England. For

6
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:49,640
the past 40 years he has been speaking

7
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:52,140
in the United States, Europe, India,

8
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:54,640
Australia, and other parts of the world.

9
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:57,020
From the outset of his life's

10
00:00:57,020 --> 00:00:59,400
work he repudiated all connections with

11
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,999
organized religions and ideologies and said that

12
00:01:01,999 --> 00:01:04,599
his only concern was to set men

13
00:01:04,599 --> 00:01:07,819
absolutely unconditionally free. He is the

14
00:01:07,819 --> 00:01:11,039
author of many books, among them the

15
00:01:11,039 --> 00:01:14,079
Awakening of Intelligence, The Urgency of

16
00:01:14,079 --> 00:01:17,120
Change, Freedom from the Known, and The

17
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:19,960
Flight of the Eagle. This is one

18
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:22,800
of a series of dialogues between Krishnamurti

19
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:24,940
and Dr. Alan W. Anderson, who

20
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:27,080
is professor of religious studies at San

21
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:29,280
Diego State University where he teaches

22
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:31,480
Indian and Chinese scriptures and the

23
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:34,500
oracular tradition. Dr. Anderson, a

24
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:37,520
published poet, received his degree from

25
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:39,760
Columbia University and the Union

26
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,000
Theological Seminary. He has been honored

27
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,160
with a Distinguished Teaching Award

28
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:48,320
from the California State Universities.

29
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:51,979
Mr. Krishnamurti, if I recall correctly, I

30
00:01:51,979 --> 00:01:55,639
think we had begun to talk together

31
00:01:55,639 --> 00:01:59,999
before, last time, just at the point where

32
00:01:59,999 --> 00:02:04,359
the question of fear arose. And I think we

33
00:02:04,359 --> 00:02:08,759
both perhaps could explore that together a little.

34
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:10,759
Yes, I think so too.

35
00:02:10,759 --> 00:02:16,479
I wonder how we can approach this problem,

36
00:02:16,479 --> 00:02:22,200
because this is a common problem in the world.

37
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:26,940
Everyone, or I can say

38
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:31,680
almost everyone, is frightened of something.

39
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:37,520
Oh, it may be the fear of death, fear of

40
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:43,360
loneliness, fear of not being loved, fear of not becoming

41
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:48,700
famous, successful, or also fear of not having

42
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:54,040
physical security. And I think we can explore

43
00:02:54,040 --> 00:03:00,719
fear of not having physical security, and

44
00:03:00,719 --> 00:03:07,399
the fear of not having psychological security.

45
00:03:07,399 --> 00:03:14,599
There are so many multiple forms of fears.

46
00:03:14,599 --> 00:03:21,799
Now, to go into this problem really very deeply,

47
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:30,660
can the mind, and which includes the

48
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:39,520
brain, be really, fundamentally be free of fear?

49
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:44,600
Because fear, as I have observed, is a dreadful thing.

50
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:46,600
Oh yes.

51
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:51,979
It darkens the world, it destroys everything. And

52
00:03:51,979 --> 00:03:57,359
I don't think we can discuss fear, which

53
00:03:57,359 --> 00:04:01,799
is one of the principles in life,

54
00:04:01,799 --> 00:04:06,240
without also discussing or going into the pursuit

55
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:11,800
of pleasure. The two are the

56
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:17,360
sides, two sides of the same coin.

57
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:23,840
Fear and pleasure, two sides of the same coin.

58
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:29,999
So as we are going to first take

59
00:04:29,999 --> 00:04:36,159
fear, there is conscious as well as unconscious fears,

60
00:04:36,159 --> 00:04:41,919
fears that are observable, that can be remedied,

61
00:04:41,919 --> 00:04:47,679
and fears that are deep rooted, deep in the

62
00:04:47,679 --> 00:04:51,359
recesses of one's mind.

63
00:04:51,359 --> 00:04:52,359
At the unconscious level.

64
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:53,840
At the deeper levels.

65
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:54,840
Yes.

66
00:04:54,840 --> 00:05:00,780
Now, we must be concerned with both, not

67
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:06,720
only the obvious external fears, but also the deep

68
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:13,780
seated, undiscovered fears. The fears that

69
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:20,840
have been handed down, traditional fears.

70
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:21,840
Being told what to fear.

71
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:25,959
And also fears that the

72
00:05:25,959 --> 00:05:29,599
mind itself has produced, has cultivated.

73
00:05:29,599 --> 00:05:30,599
In one's personal history.

74
00:05:30,599 --> 00:05:34,159
In personal, and also in relation to others.

75
00:05:34,159 --> 00:05:35,159
Yes.

76
00:05:35,159 --> 00:05:42,459
Fears of physical insecurity, losing a job,

77
00:05:42,459 --> 00:05:49,760
losing a position, losing something, and not

78
00:05:50,159 --> 00:05:53,599
or the positive is not having

79
00:05:53,599 --> 00:05:57,039
something, and so on and on.

80
00:05:57,039 --> 00:06:03,719
So if we are going to talk about this

81
00:06:03,719 --> 00:06:10,400
question, how shall we, you and I, approach this? First

82
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:18,980
the outer, the obvious physical fears, and

83
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:26,560
then from there move to the inner.

84
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:30,280
And so cover the whole field, not just one little

85
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:34,000
fear of an old lady or an old man or

86
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
a young man.

87
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,520
You take the whole problem of fear.

88
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:39,679
Good.

89
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:44,000
Not just take one leaf of fear, or one

90
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:48,320
branch of it, but the whole movement of fear.

91
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:49,320
Yes.

92
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:52,720
We are back to that word movement again.

93
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:53,720
Yes, movement of fear.

94
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:54,720
Good, good.

95
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:57,240
The whole movement of fear.

96
00:06:57,240 --> 00:07:03,540
Now outwardly, physically, it is becoming

97
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:09,840
obvious that we must have security. Physical

98
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:13,920
security, that is food, clothes, and shelter,

99
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:18,000
are absolutely necessary. Not only for the

100
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,840
Americans, for the whole humanity.

101
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:20,840
Yes, of course.

102
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:23,920
And it is no good saying we are secure and

103
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:27,000
to hell with the rest of the world. The world

104
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:30,640
is you. And you are the world. You can't

105
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:34,280
isolate yourself and say, I am going to be

106
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:38,360
secure and not bother about the others.

107
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,360
Secure myself against them.

108
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:43,840
Then it becomes a division, conflict, war,

109
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:48,320
all that produces them. So that physical security

110
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:54,160
for the brain. The brain can only function,

111
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:59,000
as I have observed it in myself, in others,

112
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,579
not that I am an expert on brain or

113
00:08:01,579 --> 00:08:04,159
neurology and all that, but I have observed it. The

114
00:08:04,159 --> 00:08:09,159
brain can function only in complete

115
00:08:09,159 --> 00:08:14,159
security. Then it functions efficiently, healthily,

116
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:18,740
not neurotically, and its actions won't

117
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:23,320
be lopsided, disheartened. The brain needs

118
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:30,080
security, as the child needs security. Now,

119
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:36,840
that security is denied when we separate ourselves.

120
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:40,980
the Americans, the Russians, the Indians,

121
00:08:40,980 --> 00:08:44,440
the Chinese, the national division has destroyed

122
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:50,560
that security. Because of wars.

123
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:53,080
Yes, that is a physical barrier.

124
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:54,080
Physical fact.

125
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,080
Yes, yes.

126
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:59,340
And yet we don't see that. Sovereign governments

127
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:03,600
with their armies, with their navies and all

128
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:08,360
the rest of it, is destroying security.

129
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:09,360
In the name of...

130
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,360
In the name of whatever.

131
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:12,360
Providing it.

132
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,360
Yes.

133
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:17,820
So, you see, what we are trying to get

134
00:09:17,820 --> 00:09:22,280
at is how stupid the mind is. It wants security

135
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:25,920
and it must have security, and yet

136
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:29,560
it is doing everything to destroy that security.

137
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:35,160
Oh yes, yes, yes, I see that.

138
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:42,900
So, that is one factor. And the factor

139
00:09:42,900 --> 00:09:50,640
of security is in jobs, either in a factory,

140
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:56,140
or as a priest in his

141
00:09:56,140 --> 00:10:00,640
job. So, occupation becomes very important.

142
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:01,640
Indeed it does.

143
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:07,500
So, see what is involved. If I lose my

144
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:13,360
job, I am frightened. And that job depends on the

145
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:20,030
environment, on the production, business,

146
00:10:20,030 --> 00:10:25,700
factory, all that commercialism, consumerism,

147
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:30,570
and therefore competition with other countries.

148
00:10:30,570 --> 00:10:35,440
France isolating itself because it wants to

149
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:37,440
which is happening.

150
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:38,440
Yes.

151
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:44,580
So, we need physical security and we are doing

152
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:50,720
everything to destroy it. If we all of us

153
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:54,180
said, look, let's all get together, not with

154
00:10:54,180 --> 00:10:57,640
plans, not my plan, your plan, or the communist

155
00:10:57,640 --> 00:11:01,020
plan, or Mao's plan, let's as human

156
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:04,400
beings sit together and solve this problem. They

157
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:08,960
could do it. Science has the means of

158
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:13,520
feeding people, but they won't because they are

159
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:19,700
conditioned to function so as to destroy security

160
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:25,880
which they are seeking. So, that is one of

161
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:37,520
the major factors in physical security. Then

162
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:49,160
there is the fear of physical pain. Physical

163
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:55,059
in the sense one has had pain, let's say,

164
00:11:55,059 --> 00:11:59,959
last week. Mind is afraid that it should happen

165
00:11:59,959 --> 00:12:06,280
again. So, there is that kind of fear.

166
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:08,540
It's very interesting with respect to the

167
00:12:08,540 --> 00:12:10,800
phenomenon of physical pain because what is

168
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:14,540
remembered is not the neurological reaction

169
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:18,280
but the emotion that attends what occurred.

170
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:23,720
That's it. So, there is that fear. Then

171
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:29,160
there is the fear of outward opinion, what people

172
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:34,079
say, public opinion.

173
00:12:34,079 --> 00:12:35,079
Reputation.

174
00:12:35,079 --> 00:12:38,579
Reputation. You see, sir, all

175
00:12:38,579 --> 00:12:42,079
this is born out of disorder.

176
00:12:42,079 --> 00:12:45,079
I don't know if I...

177
00:12:45,079 --> 00:12:46,079
Oh, yes.

178
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:47,880
Which we discussed previously.

179
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:50,200
Yes, which we looked into previously.

180
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:56,120
So, can the mind bring about security,

181
00:12:56,120 --> 00:13:02,040
physical security, which means food, clothes and shelter

182
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:08,040
for everybody, not as a communist, as a capitalist,

183
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:14,040
as a socialist, or as a Mao, but meet together

184
00:13:14,319 --> 00:13:17,819
as human beings to resolve this problem? It can

185
00:13:17,819 --> 00:13:21,319
be done, but nobody wants to do it because

186
00:13:21,319 --> 00:13:25,819
they don't feel responsible for this. I don't know

187
00:13:25,819 --> 00:13:30,319
if you have been to India, if you have

188
00:13:30,319 --> 00:13:35,079
gone from town to town to village, as I

189
00:13:35,079 --> 00:13:39,839
have done, you see the appalling poverty, the degradation

190
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:53,200
of poverty, the sense of hopelessness of it.

191
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:56,340
Yes, yes, I have been to India and it was

192
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:59,480
the first time in my life that I sensed poverty

193
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:02,120
not simply as a privation but it seemed

194
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:04,760
to have a positive character about it. It was

195
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:05,760
so stark.

196
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:08,260
I know, sir, I know. Personally

197
00:14:08,260 --> 00:14:10,760
we have been through all that.

198
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:12,760
Oh, yes.

199
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:20,680
So, physical survival is only possible when

200
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:28,600
human beings get together, not as communist,

201
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:31,180
socialist, all the rest, as human beings who

202
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:33,760
say, look, this is our problem, for God's

203
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:37,599
sake, let's solve it. But they won't

204
00:14:37,599 --> 00:14:41,439
because they are burdened with problems, with planning.

205
00:14:41,439 --> 00:14:45,000
How to solve that? I don't know if you understand.

206
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

207
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,560
You have your plan, I have my plan,

208
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:51,120
he has his plan. So planning becomes most important,

209
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:56,340
plans become most important rather than the

210
00:14:56,340 --> 00:15:01,560
starvation. And we fight each other. And common

211
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:06,759
sense, affection, care, love, control, change all this.

212
00:15:06,759 --> 00:15:11,959
So I won't go into that. Then the

213
00:15:11,959 --> 00:15:16,899
fear of public opinion. You

214
00:15:16,899 --> 00:15:21,839
understand? What my neighbour will say.

215
00:15:21,839 --> 00:15:25,640
My image, the national image, yes.

216
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:29,079
And I depend on my neighbour.

217
00:15:29,080 --> 00:15:31,080
Oh, yes.

218
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:35,940
If I am a Catholic living in Italy, I

219
00:15:35,940 --> 00:15:40,800
have to depend on my neighbour because I will lose

220
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:44,840
my job if I am a Protestant then. So I

221
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:48,880
accept it. I go and salute the Pope or whatever. It

222
00:15:48,880 --> 00:15:55,720
has no meaning. So I am afraid of public

223
00:15:55,720 --> 00:16:02,560
opinion. See what a human mind has reduced itself to.

224
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:06,660
I don't say to please us with public

225
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:10,760
opinion because they are stupid. They are conditioned,

226
00:16:11,439 --> 00:16:18,699
as much as I am. So there is that

227
00:16:18,699 --> 00:16:25,960
fear. And there is the fear, physical fear of death,

228
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:31,000
which is an immense fear. That fear one

229
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:36,040
has to tackle differently when we come to it,

230
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:39,300
when we talk about death and all that. So

231
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:42,560
there is the outward form of fear, fear of

232
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:50,220
darkness, fear of public opinion, fear of

233
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:57,880
losing a job, fear of survival, not being

234
00:16:57,880 --> 00:17:03,499
able to survive. Sir, I have lived with people with

235
00:17:03,499 --> 00:17:09,119
one meal a day and that is not enough even.

236
00:17:09,119 --> 00:17:13,399
I have walked behind a woman with a girl

237
00:17:13,399 --> 00:17:17,680
and the girl said in India, mother I am hungry.

238
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:21,700
And the mother says, you have already

239
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:25,720
eaten for the day. You understand, sir?

240
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:27,800
Yes.

241
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:33,760
So there are all that physical fears, pain

242
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:39,720
and the fear of recurring pain and that. And

243
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:44,640
there is the other fears are much more

244
00:17:44,640 --> 00:17:49,560
complicated. Fears of dependency inwardly. I depend on

245
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:55,840
my wife, I depend on my guru, I depend on

246
00:17:55,840 --> 00:18:02,120
the priest, I depend on so many dependents. And I am

247
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:06,660
afraid to lose them, to be left alone. To

248
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:11,200
be rejected. To be rejected. If that woman turns away

249
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:16,900
from me, I am lost. I get angry, brutal,

250
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:22,600
violent, jealous, because I have depended on her. So

251
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:30,240
dependency is one of the factors of fear. And

252
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:37,880
inwardly I am afraid. I am afraid of loneliness.

253
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:43,520
The other day I saw on the television a woman

254
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:49,160
saying, the only fear I have in life is my loneliness.

255
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:57,040
And therefore being afraid of loneliness I

256
00:18:57,040 --> 00:19:04,920
do all kinds of neurotic activities. Being lonely,

257
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:11,680
I attach myself to you, or to a belief, or

258
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:18,440
to a saviour, to a guru, and I protect the guru,

259
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:23,240
the saviour, the belief, and that soon becomes neurotic.

260
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:29,800
A. I fill up the hole with this new image.

261
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:30,480
K. With this rubbish.

262
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:31,000
A. Yes.

263
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:37,920
K. There is that fear. Then there is the fear

264
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:44,840
of not being able to arrive, succeed, succeed in this

265
00:19:44,840 --> 00:19:48,940
world of disorder, and succeed in the

266
00:19:48,940 --> 00:19:53,040
world of spiritual, so-called spiritual world. That's

267
00:19:53,040 --> 00:19:54,120
what they are all doing now.

268
00:19:54,120 --> 00:19:55,520
A. Spiritual achievement.

269
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:58,320
K. Achievement. Which they call enlightenment.

270
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:00,560
A. Expanding consciousness.

271
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:01,080
K. Yes.

272
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:03,820
A. I know what you mean. It's very interesting

273
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:06,560
that you just got through describing fear of being

274
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:09,200
left behind. Now we are

275
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:11,840
fearing that we will never arrive.

276
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:12,399
K. All right.

277
00:20:12,399 --> 00:20:13,600
A. Yes. Please go on.

278
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:21,040
K. Same thing. Then there is the fear

279
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:28,480
of not being, which translates itself in identification

280
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:33,360
with. I must identify myself.

281
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:36,000
A. In order to be.

282
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:42,000
K. To be. Let me identify myself with my country.

283
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:48,000
And I say to myself, that's too stupid. Then I

284
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:54,200
say I must identify myself with God, which I

285
00:20:54,200 --> 00:21:00,320
have invented. God has not made man in his image.

286
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:03,040
Man has made God in his image.

287
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:07,840
A. Yes. Oh, I follow you.

288
00:21:08,034 --> 00:21:08,534
そう

289
00:21:10,786 --> 00:21:17,546
Not being, not achieving, not arriving

290
00:21:17,546 --> 00:21:22,026
brings about tremendous sense of uncertainty,

291
00:21:22,026 --> 00:21:25,946
tremendous sense of not being able to fulfil,

292
00:21:25,946 --> 00:21:30,906
not being able to be with.

293
00:21:30,906 --> 00:21:34,946
And the cry, I must be myself.

294
00:21:34,946 --> 00:21:37,746
A. Do my own thing. K.

295
00:21:37,746 --> 00:21:40,546
My own thing, which is rubbish.

296
00:21:41,106 --> 00:21:44,386
So, there are all these fears,

297
00:21:44,386 --> 00:21:50,466
both logical fears, irrational fears, neurotic fears,

298
00:21:50,466 --> 00:21:57,546
and fears of survival, physical survival.

299
00:21:57,546 --> 00:22:03,346
So, now, how do you deal with all these fears,

300
00:22:03,346 --> 00:22:06,786
and many more fears which you can't go into,

301
00:22:06,786 --> 00:22:09,426
which we will presently.

302
00:22:09,426 --> 00:22:16,146
How do you deal with them all, one by one?

303
00:22:16,146 --> 00:22:17,626
A. Well, you would just be

304
00:22:17,626 --> 00:22:19,106
in the mournful round of fragmentation

305
00:22:19,106 --> 00:22:20,186
if you did that.

306
00:22:20,186 --> 00:22:25,066
K. And also there is the fear, hidden fears,

307
00:22:25,066 --> 00:22:28,106
which are much more active.

308
00:22:28,106 --> 00:22:31,586
A. The continual bubbling up from below.

309
00:22:31,586 --> 00:22:33,346
K. When I am not conscious they take over.

310
00:22:33,346 --> 00:22:37,186
A. That's right.

311
00:22:37,186 --> 00:22:41,946
So, how am I to deal, first,

312
00:22:41,946 --> 00:22:47,586
with the obvious fears which we have described,

313
00:22:48,506 --> 00:22:54,786
shall I deal it one by one, first secure myself?

314
00:22:54,786 --> 00:23:00,306
You follow? Or take loneliness and tackle that,

315
00:23:00,306 --> 00:23:01,646
come to grips with it,

316
00:23:01,646 --> 00:23:02,986
go beyond it, and so on?

317
00:23:02,986 --> 00:23:06,666
Or is there a way of dealing with fear,

318
00:23:06,666 --> 00:23:09,785
not with the branches of it,

319
00:23:09,785 --> 00:23:12,905
but with the root of it?

320
00:23:12,905 --> 00:23:19,386
Because if I take each leaf, each branch,

321
00:23:19,386 --> 00:23:23,226
it will take all my lifetime.

322
00:23:23,226 --> 00:23:27,865
And if I begin to analyse my fears, analyse,

323
00:23:27,865 --> 00:23:33,906
then that very analysis becomes a paralysis.

324
00:23:33,946 --> 00:23:35,466
And then I even fear that

325
00:23:35,466 --> 00:23:36,986
I might not have analysed correctly.

326
00:23:36,986 --> 00:23:40,346
K. Correct. And I am caught over and over again.

327
00:23:40,346 --> 00:23:45,266
So how shall I deal with this problem,

328
00:23:45,266 --> 00:23:48,206
as a whole, not just

329
00:23:48,206 --> 00:23:51,146
parts of it, fragments of it?

330
00:23:51,146 --> 00:23:54,506
A. Isn't there a hint about

331
00:23:54,506 --> 00:23:57,866
how it might be dealt with?

332
00:23:57,866 --> 00:24:00,526
Of course, when I say hint

333
00:24:00,526 --> 00:24:03,186
here, I mean terribly, terribly slight.

334
00:24:03,186 --> 00:24:06,226
I don't think I would call it a pointer.

335
00:24:06,226 --> 00:24:11,286
But fear, no matter how

336
00:24:11,286 --> 00:24:16,346
many varieties one imagines he knows,

337
00:24:16,346 --> 00:24:22,466
fear does have a common taste, you might say.

338
00:24:22,466 --> 00:24:24,306
There is something there.

339
00:24:24,306 --> 00:24:26,386
K. Yes, sir, but what shall I do with it?

340
00:24:26,386 --> 00:24:28,306
A. Oh yes, of course, I quite understand.

341
00:24:28,306 --> 00:24:31,666
But it interested me while you were speaking,

342
00:24:31,666 --> 00:24:41,066
to observe that already when we think of many fears,

343
00:24:41,066 --> 00:24:43,286
we haven't even paid attention to

344
00:24:43,286 --> 00:24:45,506
how we fear, when we fear.

345
00:24:45,506 --> 00:24:49,786
Yes, I was interested to have that flash,

346
00:24:49,786 --> 00:24:52,186
because it seems to be altogether consonant

347
00:24:52,186 --> 00:24:54,226
with what you're talking about.

348
00:24:54,226 --> 00:24:57,186
And I said to myself, now, in our conversations

349
00:24:57,186 --> 00:25:00,466
we've been pointing to movement.

350
00:25:00,466 --> 00:25:02,466
The movement of fear is one.

351
00:25:02,466 --> 00:25:05,346
K. Yes, a tremendous one.

352
00:25:05,346 --> 00:25:09,666
A. And it is a unified field of destruction.

353
00:25:09,666 --> 00:25:12,226
K. It is the common factor of every human being.

354
00:25:12,226 --> 00:25:15,186
A. The whole thing, yes, exactly.

355
00:25:15,186 --> 00:25:17,806
K. Whether a man lives in Moscow

356
00:25:17,806 --> 00:25:20,426
or in India or in any place,

357
00:25:20,426 --> 00:25:24,706
it is the common thing of this fear.

358
00:25:24,706 --> 00:25:29,305
And how shall he deal with it?

359
00:25:30,786 --> 00:25:37,506
Because unless the mind is free of fear,

360
00:25:37,506 --> 00:25:42,066
really, not verbally or ideologically,

361
00:25:42,066 --> 00:25:44,546
absolutely be free of fear,

362
00:25:44,546 --> 00:25:52,146
and it is possible to be free, completely of fear.

363
00:25:52,146 --> 00:25:56,946
I'm saying this not as a theory,

364
00:25:56,946 --> 00:26:01,106
but I know what I have gone into very deeply.

365
00:26:01,106 --> 00:26:03,186
A. Actual. K. Actual.

366
00:26:03,186 --> 00:26:05,826
Now, how shall I deal with this?

367
00:26:05,826 --> 00:26:10,146
So I ask myself, what is fear?

368
00:26:10,146 --> 00:26:15,026
Not the objects of fear or the expressions of fear.

369
00:26:15,026 --> 00:26:17,346
A. No, or the instant reaction to danger.

370
00:26:17,346 --> 00:26:21,186
K. Danger. What is fear?

371
00:26:21,186 --> 00:26:23,346
A. It's an idea in my mind in part.

372
00:26:23,346 --> 00:26:26,626
K. What is fear, sir?

373
00:26:32,626 --> 00:26:37,266
A. If we have said it's an abiding...

374
00:26:37,266 --> 00:26:43,666
K. No, behind the words, behind the description,

375
00:26:43,666 --> 00:26:46,866
the explanations, the way out and the way in,

376
00:26:46,866 --> 00:26:51,346
and all the rest of it, what is fear?

377
00:26:51,346 --> 00:26:54,386
How does it come?

378
00:26:54,386 --> 00:26:56,586
A. If I followed you

379
00:26:56,586 --> 00:26:58,786
through our conversations up until now,

380
00:26:58,786 --> 00:27:08,306
I'd be inclined to say that it is another expression

381
00:27:08,306 --> 00:27:13,506
of the observer's disordered relation to the observer.

382
00:27:13,506 --> 00:27:15,986
K. What does that mean? What is the observer?

383
00:27:16,066 --> 00:27:22,066
What you say... Look, the problem is this.

384
00:27:22,066 --> 00:27:26,786
I'm only making the problem clearer so that we can...

385
00:27:26,786 --> 00:27:32,146
We have... Man has tried to lop off or prune

386
00:27:32,146 --> 00:27:42,066
one fear after the other, through analysis, through escape,

387
00:27:42,145 --> 00:27:45,585
through identifying himself with something

388
00:27:45,585 --> 00:27:51,186
which he calls courage, or saying,

389
00:27:51,186 --> 00:27:53,666
I don't care, I rationalise my fears

390
00:27:53,666 --> 00:27:57,265
and remain in a state of rationalised, intellectual,

391
00:27:57,265 --> 00:28:03,505
verbal explanation, but the thing is boiling.

392
00:28:03,505 --> 00:28:07,585
So what shall I do?

393
00:28:07,585 --> 00:28:11,825
What is fear?

394
00:28:11,826 --> 00:28:19,186
Unless I find this out, not because you tell me,

395
00:28:19,186 --> 00:28:22,146
unless I find it out for myself,

396
00:28:22,146 --> 00:28:26,226
as I find for myself that I am hungry.

397
00:28:26,226 --> 00:28:30,066
Nobody has to tell me I'm hungry.

398
00:28:30,066 --> 00:28:33,746
I have to find this out.

399
00:28:33,746 --> 00:28:35,986
A. Yes, now there's a difference here

400
00:28:35,986 --> 00:28:40,866
in terms of what you have just said,

401
00:28:40,866 --> 00:28:45,186
and in so saying, pointing to something.

402
00:28:45,186 --> 00:28:48,306
And my earlier reply, when

403
00:28:48,306 --> 00:28:51,426
you asked me what is fear,

404
00:28:51,426 --> 00:28:53,346
I did the usual academic thing.

405
00:28:53,346 --> 00:28:56,306
If I have followed you up until now,

406
00:28:56,306 --> 00:29:00,786
then it seems clear that...

407
00:29:00,786 --> 00:29:06,866
Whereas, let's forget about the following,

408
00:29:06,866 --> 00:29:10,385
let's zero in on it right now,

409
00:29:10,386 --> 00:29:14,626
and then I must say, not I might say,

410
00:29:14,626 --> 00:29:22,306
but I must say that I can't tell anybody else

411
00:29:22,306 --> 00:29:24,786
what fear is with respect to what it is

412
00:29:24,786 --> 00:29:27,666
I am going to discover in me as such,

413
00:29:27,666 --> 00:29:31,586
and all my continual descriptions about it

414
00:29:31,586 --> 00:29:36,946
are simply a deflection from my immediate issue,

415
00:29:36,946 --> 00:29:38,066
which is here.

416
00:29:38,066 --> 00:29:42,705
Yes. So, I am not escaping.

417
00:29:42,705 --> 00:29:43,825
A. No.

418
00:29:43,825 --> 00:29:47,906
K. I am not rationalising.

419
00:29:47,906 --> 00:29:53,585
I am not analysing, because analysis is real paralysis.

420
00:29:53,585 --> 00:29:55,985
A. Yes, indeed.

421
00:29:55,985 --> 00:29:58,625
K. When you are confronted with a problem like this,

422
00:29:58,625 --> 00:30:01,105
merely spinning over and on analysing,

423
00:30:01,105 --> 00:30:06,225
and the fear of not being able to analyse perfectly,

424
00:30:06,226 --> 00:30:09,186
and therefore go to a

425
00:30:09,186 --> 00:30:12,146
professional who needs also an analysis.

426
00:30:12,146 --> 00:30:15,346
So I am caught. So I will not analyse,

427
00:30:15,346 --> 00:30:19,986
because I see the absurdity of it.

428
00:30:19,986 --> 00:30:21,346
You follow, sir? A. Yes, I do.

429
00:30:21,346 --> 00:30:23,586
K. I won't run.

430
00:30:23,586 --> 00:30:26,546
A. No backing off, no flight.

431
00:30:26,546 --> 00:30:31,266
K. No explanations, no rationalisation, no analysis.

432
00:30:31,266 --> 00:30:35,346
I am faced with this thing.

433
00:30:35,426 --> 00:30:39,265
And what is fear?

434
00:30:39,265 --> 00:30:43,745
Wait a minute. Leave that for the moment.

435
00:30:43,745 --> 00:30:48,786
Then there are the unconscious fears,

436
00:30:48,786 --> 00:30:54,385
of which I don't know.

437
00:30:54,385 --> 00:30:59,666
They express themselves occasionally when I am alert,

438
00:30:59,666 --> 00:31:04,625
when I see this thing coming out of me.

439
00:31:04,626 --> 00:31:06,506
A. When I am alert.

440
00:31:06,506 --> 00:31:08,386
K. Alert. When I am watching.

441
00:31:08,386 --> 00:31:13,626
Or when I am looking

442
00:31:13,626 --> 00:31:18,866
at something, this comes up, uninvited.

443
00:31:20,626 --> 00:31:25,506
Now, it is important for the

444
00:31:25,506 --> 00:31:30,386
mind to be completely free of fear.

445
00:31:30,386 --> 00:31:34,066
It is essential, as food is essential.

446
00:31:34,066 --> 00:31:35,826
It is essential for the

447
00:31:35,826 --> 00:31:37,586
mind to be free of fear.

448
00:31:37,586 --> 00:31:41,346
So I see outwardly what we have discussed,

449
00:31:41,346 --> 00:31:45,266
now I say, what are the hidden fears?

450
00:31:45,266 --> 00:31:51,985
Can I consciously invite them to come to the surface?

451
00:31:51,985 --> 00:31:54,865
You follow? A. Yes, I do.

452
00:31:54,865 --> 00:32:02,225
K. Or the unconscious cannot touch that.

453
00:32:02,386 --> 00:32:05,106
You follow? A. Yes, I do.

454
00:32:05,106 --> 00:32:11,346
K. Conscious can only deal with the things it knows,

455
00:32:11,346 --> 00:32:17,826
but it cannot observe the thing it doesn't know.

456
00:32:17,826 --> 00:32:19,986
A. Or have access to.

457
00:32:19,986 --> 00:32:25,106
K. So, what am I to do? Dreams?

458
00:32:25,106 --> 00:32:27,626
Dreams are merely a continuation of

459
00:32:27,626 --> 00:32:30,146
what I have lived during the day.

460
00:32:30,146 --> 00:32:31,986
They continue in a different form.

461
00:32:31,986 --> 00:32:35,426
We won't go into that for the moment.

462
00:32:35,426 --> 00:32:43,746
So how is all that to be awakened and exposed?

463
00:32:43,746 --> 00:32:53,026
The racial fears, the fears that society has taught me,

464
00:32:53,026 --> 00:32:59,906
the fears that the family has imposed,

465
00:32:59,986 --> 00:33:03,546
the neighbour, all those crawling,

466
00:33:03,546 --> 00:33:07,106
ugly, brutal things that are hidden,

467
00:33:07,106 --> 00:33:11,026
how shall they all come up naturally

468
00:33:11,026 --> 00:33:17,666
and expose so that the mind sees them completely?

469
00:33:17,666 --> 00:33:20,066
You understand? A. Yes, I do.

470
00:33:20,066 --> 00:33:24,386
I was just thinking about what we are doing

471
00:33:24,386 --> 00:33:26,546
in relation to what you are saying.

472
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:32,386
Here we are in a university situation

473
00:33:32,386 --> 00:33:35,706
where hardly any listening goes

474
00:33:35,706 --> 00:33:39,026
on at all, if any. Why?

475
00:33:39,026 --> 00:33:41,026
Well, if we were to relate to each other

476
00:33:41,026 --> 00:33:45,266
in terms of my sitting back here,

477
00:33:45,266 --> 00:33:49,506
saying to myself every time you made a statement,

478
00:33:49,506 --> 00:33:56,146
well, what do I have to say back?

479
00:33:56,306 --> 00:33:58,866
Even if my reaction were benign,

480
00:33:58,866 --> 00:34:01,026
and I'd say to myself as a professor,

481
00:34:01,026 --> 00:34:03,906
I'd say, well, now, that's a very interesting concept.

482
00:34:03,906 --> 00:34:05,986
Perhaps we could clear that

483
00:34:05,986 --> 00:34:08,065
up a little bit, you know?

484
00:34:08,065 --> 00:34:10,226
That nonsense.

485
00:34:10,226 --> 00:34:12,946
Nonsense in terms of what is immediate here.

486
00:34:12,946 --> 00:34:13,985
That's what I mean.

487
00:34:13,985 --> 00:34:18,386
I don't mean demonstrating something on the board.

488
00:34:18,386 --> 00:34:23,585
We should never have begun to be together.

489
00:34:23,585 --> 00:34:25,906
Never have started.

490
00:34:25,906 --> 00:34:28,866
And yet we might have given ourselves the idea

491
00:34:28,866 --> 00:34:32,386
that we were trying very hard to be sincere.

492
00:34:32,386 --> 00:34:35,505
Yes, I understand.

493
00:34:35,505 --> 00:34:37,266
But fear is at the base of that too,

494
00:34:37,266 --> 00:34:40,946
because the professor is thinking to himself,

495
00:34:40,946 --> 00:34:44,226
he's got his reputation at stake here,

496
00:34:44,226 --> 00:34:46,226
he better not keep quiet too long

497
00:34:46,226 --> 00:34:47,826
because someone might get the idea

498
00:34:47,826 --> 00:34:50,226
that either he doesn't understand the thing that's going on,

499
00:34:50,226 --> 00:34:52,346
or he doesn't have anything

500
00:34:52,346 --> 00:34:54,466
to contribute to what's going on,

501
00:34:54,466 --> 00:34:56,545
all of which has nothing to do with anything.

502
00:34:56,545 --> 00:34:57,586
K. Absolutely.

503
00:34:57,586 --> 00:35:02,225
So, look, sir, what I have found.

504
00:35:02,225 --> 00:35:07,745
I cannot... the conscious mind, conscious thought,

505
00:35:07,745 --> 00:35:13,186
cannot invite and expose the hidden fears.

506
00:35:13,186 --> 00:35:16,625
It cannot analyse it,

507
00:35:16,625 --> 00:35:21,666
because that analysis we said is inaction.

508
00:35:21,666 --> 00:35:24,066
And if there is no escape,

509
00:35:24,066 --> 00:35:27,426
I shan't run off to a

510
00:35:27,426 --> 00:35:30,786
church, or Jesus, or Buddha, or somebody,

511
00:35:30,786 --> 00:35:34,466
or identify myself with some other thing,

512
00:35:34,466 --> 00:35:37,026
I've pushed all those aside

513
00:35:37,026 --> 00:35:45,186
because I've understood their futility.

514
00:35:45,186 --> 00:35:49,426
So I'm left with this.

515
00:35:49,426 --> 00:35:52,306
I'm this, my baby.

516
00:35:52,306 --> 00:35:56,066
A. Yes. Right.

517
00:35:56,066 --> 00:36:01,266
K. So, what shall I do?

518
00:36:04,386 --> 00:36:05,985
Some action has to take place.

519
00:36:05,985 --> 00:36:07,186
A. Yes, indeed.

520
00:36:07,186 --> 00:36:08,346
K. I can't just say,

521
00:36:08,346 --> 00:36:09,506
well, I've pushed all that aside,

522
00:36:09,506 --> 00:36:11,746
I'll just sit.

523
00:36:11,746 --> 00:36:14,225
Now, just see what happens, sir.

524
00:36:14,225 --> 00:36:18,066
Because I've pushed all those aside,

525
00:36:18,066 --> 00:36:20,986
through observation, not through

526
00:36:20,986 --> 00:36:23,906
resistance, not through violence,

527
00:36:23,906 --> 00:36:27,105
